<h3>The 12-week cycle: Specific sharpening</h3>

<p>Twelve weeks is the optimal timeframe for peak performance if the base work is already done. It is a direct, aggressive, and specific block.</p>

<p>Starting in September carries a massive thermal advantage. Your first load week aligns with dropping temperatures, allowing your quality sessions to be precise from day one. By skipping the initial six-week build, you reduce the probability of chronic overuse injuries by a third.</p>

<p>In this block, the focus shifts rapidly from simple kilometer accumulation to extending the time you can spend near your threshold and at your target marathon pace.</p>

